ngp: --minify-styles, minified component styles for production builds

The Angular CLI minifies component styles when optimization.styles is on
(production). ngp inlined them expanded, so a production bundle carried
unminified CSS and component-style budgets measured more than `ng build`.

With --minify-styles, the style preprocessor emits compressed CSS: Sass
stylesheets compile with style "compressed", plain CSS goes through Sass's CSS
syntax. A stylesheet Sass cannot parse as plain CSS, or a workspace without
`sass`, keeps the original CSS instead of failing the build. Minification
happens before view encapsulation, as with the Angular CLI.

Applies on top of 0001-ngp-compile-sass-component-styles.patch.

